on. Or ask Agent 3 for crew cooperation evidence for A, C, D. But we can also give our own perspective: I think Candidate C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and leadership is strong, but concerns about criticism and organization. Might propose that C could be better if feedback orientation improves.\n\nWe need to decide whether to keep vote B or shift. According to guidelines, we should consider all candidates before final. We could keep vote B but ask for more info on crew cooperation for B and others. Or we could shift to A if we think A's reliability and positive atmosphere outweigh B's communication issues.\n\nOur own notes: Candidate A known 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, can be grumpy, can be uncooperative. Wait note says B can be grumpy and uncooperative (contradicts earlier note of pretentious). So B has cooperation concerns. Candidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership.\n\nThus B has both communication and cooperation concerns. A has egocentric and communication difficulty but is reliable and positive atmosphere. C has leadership but criticism and organization issues. D has responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWe might argue that A's reliability and positive crew atmosphere outweigh his egocentric trait, and his decision speed is crucial for long-distance. B's cooperation issues may be more problematic. So we could shift vote to A.\n\nWe need to reference the discussion: Agents 2 and 3 have advocated B. We can challenge that, citing B's uncooperative behavior and grumpiness, which may affect crew cooperation, a key criterion. Meanwhile A is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere, which is strong for crew cooperation. So we could propose A.\n\nLet's craft: \"I appreciate the points for B, but I have concerns about his uncooperative and grumpy behavior, which could undermine crew cooperation. In contrast, Candidate A is known to be 100% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, indicating strong crew cooperation despite his egocentric tendencies. Therefore I think A may be a better overall fit.\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: A known 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere; B can be grumpy, uncooperative. Also mention A can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality). Also note A's difficulty communicating ideas but maybe less severe than B's tone? We can argue.\n\nThus vote A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate A."}
